(Ministry sees no plan to restrict rice exports) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P1] The Realm Trade Ministry said today that it has no plan to restrict rice) Tj
T*
(exports.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P2] The ministry said it was monitoring the harvest and domestic prices but saw) Tj
T*
(no reason to change the current rules.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P3] Vanir's rice exports continue under the existing arrangements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P4] The ministry will review the position if market conditions change.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P5] Exporters should continue to work to the current rules.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P6] The statement was issued after a routine review of export policy and was) Tj
T*
(not caused by any single shipment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P7] The ministry said it would continue to consult producers and buyers before) Tj
T*
(any change.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P8] Exporters said the current arrangements had been in place for some time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P9] The notice was published in the usual gazette and is still available in the) Tj
T*
(archive.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P10] The ministry said it would give exporters notice before any new rule took) Tj
T*
(effect.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P11] The harvest was still being assessed at the time of the statement.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
